hine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"match-binomial-head-counts","label":"Match binomial head counts","methodDirectNodeIds":{"match-binomial-head-counts":["cnm_h255","cnm_h138"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h255","cnm_h138"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:6f61f9d66cab17611309f95d"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A. m = 243; probability = 243/1024","reason":"Fix a red set of size k. Independence requires the red-striped count i and blue-striped count j to satisfy (6-k)i = kj. For k = 0 through 6, the numbers of stripe assignments are 64, 2, 14, 20, 14, 2, 64. Weighting by C(6,k) gives 972 favorable outcomes out of 4^6 = 4096. Thus the probability is 243/1024, with numerator 243.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h255"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2024_AMC_12B_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"condition-on-red-count","label":"Condition on the number of red balls","methodDirectNodeIds":{"condition-on-red-count":["cnm_h140","cnm_h137","cnm_h255","cnm_h246"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h255","cnm_h246","cnm_h140","cnm_h137"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:6f61f9d66cab17611309f95d"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B (5/36)","reason":"Mel and Chelsea have probabilities 1/3 and 1/6. There are 6!/(3!2!1!) = 60 qualifying sequences, each with probability (1/2)^3(1/3)^2(1/6) = 1/432. The total is 60/432 = 5/36.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h255"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2012_AMC_12A_Q11","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"conditional-binomial-counts","label":"Conditional binomial counts","methodDirectNodeIds":{"conditional-binomial-counts":["cnm_h255","cnm_h244","cnm_h245"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h255","cnm_h244","cnm_h245"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:6f61f9d66cab17611309f95d"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, 220/3^10","reason":"If k selections have modulus √2, then |P|=2^(3k/2-12), so |P|=1 requires k=8. This has probability C(12,8)(1/3)^8(2/3)^4. Conditional on this event, the four smaller factors make the product's argument uniform among the four multiples of π/2. Thus P(P=-1)=C(12,8)(1/3)^8(2/3)^4/4=220/3^10.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h255"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2017_AMC_12A_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"polar-phase-count","label":"Moduli and arguments","methodDirectNodeIds":{"polar-phase-count":["math:complex-polar-de-moivre","cnm_h255"]},"nodeIds":["math:complex-polar-de-moivre","cnm_h255"]}]}],"canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h255"],"label":"二项分布","layer":"CN","meaning":"Practice covers aligned canonical concepts, with no claim of complete standard coverage or mastery.","nextOffset":null,"sourceNode":{"criteria":["能计算二项分布的一个概率","能说出 X 表示成功次数"],"description":"n 重伯努利试验中，成功次数 X 服从二项分布。P(X=k)=C(n,k) p^k (1−p)^(n−k)。","id":"cnm_h255","label":"二项分布","original":{"chapter":"选必三 第七章 随机变量及其分布 7.4","description":"n 重伯努利试验中，成功次数 X 服从二项分布。P(X=k)=C(n,k) p^k (1−p)^(n−k)。","domain":"统计与概率","external":false,"grade":14,"id":"cnm_h255","mastery_criteria":["能计算二项分布的一个概率","能说出 X 表示成功次数"],"name":"二项分布","semester":"上","standards":[{"confidence":"exact","id":"cms-2017:H.PS.15"}],"type":"procedural"},"placement":{"bookCode":"14","bookLabel":"选必三","chapter":"选必三 第七章 随机变量及其分布 7.4","domain":"统计与概率","semester":"上"},"reviewStatus":"source_only"},"sourceNodeId":"cnm_h255","status":"mapped","total":21}
